#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_ACTION.rst:2
msgid "CMAKE_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_ACTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/include/ENV_VAR.rst:1
msgid ""
"This is a CMake :ref:`Environment Variable <CMake Language Environment "
"Variables>`. Its initial value is taken from the calling process environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_ACTION.rst:8
msgid ""
"Specify the action taken by :manual:`cmake(1)` when the value of :envvar:"
"`CMAKE_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_ID` in the environment does not match the cached "
"value. If not set, the default is ``WARN``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_ACTION.rst:12
msgid "The value may be one of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_ACTION.rst:14
msgid "``IGNORE``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_ACTION.rst:15
msgid "No action is taken."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_ACTION.rst:17
msgid "``WARN``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_ACTION.rst:18
msgid "A warning is emitted to the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_ACTION.rst:20
msgid "``REFRESH``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_ACTION.rst:21
msgid ""
"The cache is automatically refreshed, as if by :cmake-option:`--fresh`. Take "
"care when setting this option, as all cache variables not specified in a "
"configure preset or the current invocation of :manual:`cmake(1)` will be "
"lost."
msgstr ""
